Route the GTree key comparator through a correctly-typed function.

mc builds its event-group and event trees with

    g_tree_new_full ((GCompareDataFunc) g_ascii_strcasecmp, ...)

g_ascii_strcasecmp takes two parameters; GCompareDataFunc takes three
(key_a, key_b, user_data). Calling a function through a pointer of an
incompatible type is undefined behaviour in C, and the cast only appears
to work because mainstream native ABIs let the callee ignore an argument
the caller pushed.

WebAssembly does not. call_indirect carries the static type of the call
site and every engine traps when the referenced function's type differs,
so the first g_tree_lookup during events_init aborted the process:

    null function or function signature mismatch
      at g_tree_lookup
      at mc_event_get_event_group_by_name
      at mc_event_add / mc_event_mass_add / events_init / main

This is not a Kandelo limitation being worked around: no WebAssembly
engine can dispatch a two-parameter function through a three-parameter
type, so the defect is in mc's cast. glib's own port carries the same
fix for its internal GCompareFunc-as-GCompareDataFunc casts.

Adds one wrapper with the exact GCompareDataFunc signature and uses it
at both tree-construction sites.

--- a/lib/event/internal.h
+++ b/lib/event/internal.h
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 
 /*** declarations of public functions **********************************/
 
+gint mc_event_key_compare (gconstpointer a, gconstpointer b, gpointer user_data);
 GTree *mc_event_get_event_group_by_name (const gchar * event_group_name, gboolean create_new,
                                          GError ** mcerror);
 GPtrArray *mc_event_get_event_by_name (GTree * event_group, const gchar * event_name,
--- a/lib/event/event.c
+++ b/lib/event/event.c
@@ -47,6 +47,21 @@
 /*** public functions ****************************************************************************/
 /* --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
 
+/**
+ * Compare two string keys of an event GTree.
+ *
+ * Exists so the comparator has the exact GCompareDataFunc signature.
+ * Casting g_ascii_strcasecmp (two parameters) to GCompareDataFunc (three)
+ * is undefined behaviour that native ABIs happen to tolerate; WebAssembly
+ * type-checks every indirect call and traps on it.
+ */
+gint
+mc_event_key_compare (gconstpointer a, gconstpointer b, gpointer user_data)
+{
+    (void) user_data;
+    return g_ascii_strcasecmp ((const gchar *) a, (const gchar *) b);
+}
+
 gboolean
 mc_event_init (GError **mcerror)
 {
@@ -59,7 +74,7 @@
     }
 
     mc_event_grouplist =
-        g_tree_new_full ((GCompareDataFunc) g_ascii_strcasecmp,
+        g_tree_new_full (mc_event_key_compare,
                          NULL, (GDestroyNotify) g_free, (GDestroyNotify) g_tree_destroy);
 
     if (mc_event_grouplist == NULL)
--- a/lib/event/manage.c
+++ b/lib/event/manage.c
@@ -157,7 +157,7 @@
     if (event_group == NULL && create_new)
     {
         event_group =
-            g_tree_new_full ((GCompareDataFunc) g_ascii_strcasecmp,
+            g_tree_new_full (mc_event_key_compare,
                              NULL,
                              (GDestroyNotify) g_free,
                              (GDestroyNotify) mc_event_group_destroy_value);
